### 6.2 Nesting Levels

Components should use appropriate nesting levels based on their usage context. Common nesting levels include:
- **area**: Top-level container
- **box**: Section container  
- **inline**: Inline content
- **spot**: Small inline elements

**Note**: Use sensible defaults unless user specifies different nesting level requirements.

### 6.3 State Management

Use appropriate hooks:
- `useState` - Local component state
- `useDataList` - List data with pagination
- `useDataObject` - Single object data
- `useEffect` - Side effects and lifecycle

For detailed implementation patterns, see [Visual Component Guide](mdc:docs/uu5/visual-component-guide.md).

### 6.4 ESLint Fix
> After completing component implementation and integration, you MUST run eslint fix to resolve any linting errors:
> 
> **Run ESLint Fix**:
> ```bash
> # Option 1: Direct eslint command
> npx eslint src/ --fix
> 
> # Option 2: Using project-specific eslint config
> npx eslint "src/**/*.js" --fix
> ```
> 
> **Verify ESLint Results**:
> - Check that all linting errors are resolved
> - Ensure code follows project style guidelines
> - Verify no new warnings are introduced
> - Confirm all files pass linting checks
> 
> **If ESLint errors persist**:
> - Review and fix any remaining manual errors
> - Check for configuration issues
> - Ensure all imports and dependencies are correct
> - Re-run eslint fix until all errors are resolved
> 
> **Purpose**: Ensures the visual component code follows project standards and is free of linting errors before completion.

## 7. Naming Conventions

### 7.1 Dot Notation for Module Specification

**IMPORTANT**: Users can specify both component name and module using dot notation.

| Input Format | Module Path | Component Name | File Location |
|--------------|-------------|----------------|---------------|
| `UserProfile` | Must be specified separately | `UserProfile` | `[module]/user-profile.js` |
| `User.Profile` | `user/` | `Profile` | `user/profile.js` |
| `Internal.User.Profile` | `internal/user/` | `Profile` | `internal/user/profile.js` |

**Rules**:
1. **No dots** = Component name only, user must specify module separately
2. **One dot** = `Module.Component` format, module is derived from first part
3. **Multiple dots** = `Module1.Module2.Component` format, creates nested module structure

**Examples with Location Inference**:

```
Example 1: Auction.Progress (with inference)
- Workspace: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/, uu_frontend_aicodingg01-core/
- Component name: Progress
- Inferred location: uuSubApp (because "Auction" is domain-specific)
- Confirmation: "I suggest uuSubApp because 'Auction' appears to be application-specific. Is this correct?"
- User confirms: Yes
- Module: auction/
- Type: simple (default - no confirmation needed)
- Result: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/src/auction/progress.js

Example 2: User.Detail (with inference)
- Workspace: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/, uu_frontend_aicodingg01-core/
- Component name: Detail
- Inferred location: uuSubApp (domain-specific, default)
- Confirmation: "I suggest uuSubApp for User.Detail. Is this correct, or should I use uu5Lib?"
- User corrects: "Use uu5Lib core"
- Module: user/
- Type: Name suggests "detail" type → Ask user to confirm
- Result: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-core/src/user/detail.js

Example 3: GenericButton (with inference)
- Workspace: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/, uu_frontend_aicodingg01-bricks/
- Component name: GenericButton
- Inferred location: uu5Lib (bricks) (because "Generic" suggests reusable component)
- Confirmation: "I suggest uu5Lib bricks because 'GenericButton' appears to be a reusable component. Is this correct?"
- User confirms: Yes
- Module: Must ask user (e.g., "generic-button")
- Type: simple (default - no confirmation needed)
- Result: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-bricks/src/generic-button/generic-button.js

Example 4: UserProfile (only uuSubApp exists)
- Workspace: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/
- Component name: UserProfile
- Inferred location: uuSubApp (only package available)
- Confirmation: "I suggest uuSubApp because it's the only package available. Is this correct?"
- User confirms: Yes
- Module: Must ask user (e.g., "user-profile")
- Type: simple (default - no confirmation needed)
- Result: uu_frontend_aicodingg01-hi/src/user-profile/user-profile.js
```

### 7.2 General Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Component name | PascalCase | `UserCard`, `ProductList`, `Profile` |
| File name | kebab-case | `user-card.js`, `product-list.js`, `profile.js` |
| Module name | kebab-case | `user-card/`, `product-list/`, `user/` |
| Variables/functions | camelCase | `handleClick`, `userData` |
| Constants | UPPER_CASE | `MAX_ITEMS`, `DEFAULT_TITLE` |

**File naming rules**:
- Main component: `component-name.js`
- Content: `content.js`
- Config: `config/config.js`
- Test: `component-name.test.js`

For detailed guidelines, see [Naming Conventions](mdc:docs/general-rules/naming-conventions.md).

## 8. Testing Requirements

All components must have tests covering:
- ✅ Component rendering with different props
- ✅ User interactions (clicks, inputs, etc.)
- ✅ Error states and error handling
- ✅ Loading states
- ✅ Edge cases and boundary conditions

**Optional test coverage** (only if specified by user or relevant to component):
- ✅ Different nesting levels
- ✅ Route integration
- ✅ LSI translations

For complete testing patterns and examples, see [UU5 Test Guide](mdc:docs/uu5/uu5-test-guide.md).

