## 10. Troubleshooting

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| **Workspace analysis failed** | Unable to list workspace root or packages | Check workspace path • Verify file system permissions • List workspace root manually • Ask user to specify location directly |
| **Incorrect location inferred** | Inference logic didn't match user's intent | Always confirm inferred location with user • Accept user corrections gracefully • Update inference if user provides better reasoning |
| **Package not found** | Invalid package name or directory doesn't exist | Follow complete inference process • List workspace directories • Verify package exists • Ask user to clarify location |
| **User disagrees with inference** | Different understanding of component purpose | Present inference as suggestion, not decision • Accept user's choice • Learn from correction for future inferences |
| **Multiple matching packages** | Unclear which package to use | Present all options to user • Explain differences between uuSubApp and uu5Lib • Ask user which one fits their needs |
| **Component not rendering** | Nesting level incompatibility or incorrect props | Check nesting level compatibility • Verify props are passed correctly • Check console for errors |
| **ContentContainer not working** | Incorrect import or improper usage | Verify import from `uu_plus4u5g02-elements` • Check `splitProps` is called correctly • Ensure `nestingLevelList` is provided |
| **Props not updating** | Component not re-rendering properly | Check component re-rendering logic • Verify state management • Check for reference equality issues |
| **Tests failing** | Incorrect test setup or mock data | Verify test setup • Check mock data matches expected structure • Handle async operations properly |
| **Nesting level errors** | Unsupported nesting level used | Verify parent component supports the nesting level • Check `nestingLevel` array definition |
| **CSS not applying** | CSS module not configured correctly | Check config file • Verify CSS import • Ensure TAG is properly defined |

**Debugging Tips**:
- Use React DevTools to inspect component hierarchy and props
- Add strategic console.log statements for debugging state
- Use browser debugger breakpoints for step-through debugging
- Check existing similar components in codebase for reference
- Review workspace structure to understand available packages
- Compare inferred location with similar existing components

